# Use-case to service request mapping

The API controller layer and use-case query/command records must stay independent of `*Service*Request` types defined in Core/Implementation service projects.

```csharp
// ✅ GOOD — controller maps API model to flat use-case query
new SearchUploadRecordsQuery(
    request.PageSize,
    request.CreatedBeforeUtc,
    /* ... */,
    uploadedByUserId,
    request.ContinuationToken)

// ✅ GOOD — handler maps query to service request
return await uploadService.SearchAsync(new UploadServiceSearchRequest
{
    PageSize = query.PageSize,
    UploadedByUserId = query.UploadedByUserId,
    /* ... */
}, query.ContinuationToken, cancellationToken);

// ❌ BAD — controller constructs a service request
new SearchUploadRecordsQuery(new UploadServiceSearchRequest { /* ... */ }, token)

// ❌ BAD — query embeds a service request type
public sealed record SearchUploadRecordsQuery(UploadServiceSearchRequest Parameters, Guid? ContinuationToken);
```

- **Controllers** bind `Models/{Resource}/*Request` and construct use-case queries/commands with primitive/flat fields only.
- **Use-case handlers** translate queries/commands into `*Service*Request` (or equivalent data-store requests) before calling services.
- Follow `SearchProductRecordsQuery` / `SearchUploadRecordsQuery` as the reference pattern for search endpoints.
